# Push to live

When the user says **Push to live**, **push live**, **deploy live to GitHub**, **go live**, or **push all changes**:

1. Draft a **work-based** commit message from what was actually implemented (include Change ID when one exists), e.g. `perf(admin): cut dashboard Supabase request storms [CHG-2026-2209-002]`.
2. Run immediately (do not ask for confirmation):

```bash
npm run push:live -- "type(scope): short description of the work [CHG-ID]"
```

3. Do **not** use `updates changelogs DDMMYYYY` or any other generic subject.
4. Report the commit hash, message, and whether the push succeeded.

If there is nothing to commit, still push if the branch is ahead; say so clearly.
